  "description": "Swung boom-bap hip-hop in Eb major (I-vi-ii-V: Ebmaj7 Cm9 Fm9 Bb13, jazz chords, not a minor loop) at 90 bpm. The sixteenths swing hard (0.56) and every part is humanized, so the kit sits behind the beat. A sampled jazz kit: the kick skips around a snare fixed on 2 and 4 (one on the 1, two pushed late in the bar), hats with ghosted in-betweens and accents, an open hat closing each four-bar phrase, a snare-and-kick fill in the last bar. A round sub bass written as notes (it leaves space for the kick and anticipates the next chord). FM electric piano chords through a chorus, voiced close and pushed off the beat. A bell motif answers in the hook only; the second verse drops the hook's motif and thins the kit; a four-bar drum break before the last hook; the outro takes the drums away.",
